<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE TECH UNITS TO MERGE SHARE TRANCHES.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE TECH UNITS TO MERGE SHARE TRANCHES.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four listed units of the Singapore Technologies group will merge their foreign and local share tranches effective August 14, 1997, a spokesperson for ST Aerospace said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Effective Thursday, all the dual listing units -- ST Shipbuilding and Engineering, ST Electronics &amp; Engineering, ST Automotive and ST Aerospace -- will be merging their foreign and local tranches,&quot; Shirley Tan, head of corporate communications at ST Aerospace told Reuters.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the local tranches of ST Shipbuilding ended unchanged at Singapore $1.67, ST Electronics ended one cent up at S$1.48, ST Automotive was up 12 cents at S$3.00 and ST Aerospace rose five cents to S$2.07.  </p>
<p>-- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
